WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.970
OT topologies connect physical processes with control, supervision, engineering, operations, and enterprise functions.

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:13.939
At the field level, sensors measure process conditions and actuators create physical action.

00:00:13.939 --> 00:00:20.909
Controllers such as PLCs and RTUs read inputs, execute logic, and update outputs.

00:00:20.909 --> 00:00:26.917
Human-machine interfaces give operators visibility into status, alarms, trends, and commands.

00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:32.445
SCADA systems coordinate monitoring and supervisory control across distributed assets.

00:00:32.445 --> 00:00:37.973
Distributed control systems support coordinated control within plants or processes.

00:00:37.973 --> 00:00:44.462
Engineering workstations configure controllers and applications, while historians store time-series operational data.

00:00:44.462 --> 00:00:54.315
These systems also connect to site services and enterprise applications for scheduling, reporting, maintenance, identity, remote support, and analytics.

00:00:54.315 --> 00:01:10.418
Purdue-style layers can provide a useful mental model for these functions, but the actual environment may include cloud platforms, wireless devices, vendor appliances, remote sites, and legacy links that cross traditional boundaries.

00:01:10.418 --> 00:01:14.503
Topology matters because communication paths shape risk.

00:01:14.503 --> 00:01:25.799
A reporting flow from a historian to an enterprise application has different consequences from an engineering path that can modify controller logic.

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:34.692
A remote support connection may bypass expected boundaries if it uses a separate cellular or vendor-managed service.

00:01:34.692 --> 00:01:44.065
Accurate diagrams should show assets, trust boundaries, data and control flows, remote access, dependencies, redundancy, and external connections.

00:01:44.065 --> 00:01:50.073
This information supports segmentation, monitoring placement, vulnerability analysis, and incident containment.

00:01:50.073 --> 00:02:00.888
During response, teams need to know which functions can continue locally and what may be lost when a connection is isolated.

00:02:00.888 --> 00:02:06.416
Security architecture begins with understanding how the operation actually communicates.
